cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AutoCyberGraph in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "AutoCyberGraph: Connect Automotive Cybersecurity Risk to Reality"
authors:
  - family-names: Banik
    given-names: Nirjhar
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nirjharb/AutoCyberGraph"
url: "https://github.com/nirjharb/AutoCyberGraph"
abstract: >-
  Open-source automotive cybersecurity digital-thread and evidence-graph
  platform connecting TARA, cybersecurity requirements, security controls,
  AUTOSAR security mechanisms, tests, vulnerabilities, SBOMs and release
  evidence, with graph-based change impact analysis and cybersecurity release
  gates. Reference/mapping layers for ISO/SAE 21434, UNECE R155/R156 and
  NIST SP 800-53.
keywords:
  - automotive cybersecurity
  - iso-sae-21434
  - un-r155
  - un-r156
  - tara
  - traceability
  - evidence graph
  - digital thread
  - sbom
  - change impact analysis
